#hasheq((reviewer . "independent read-only reviewer subagents (fresh non-author, reviewer role, model deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash; two rounds, a new session per round)") (verdict . "APPROVED") (reviewed-sha . "220f676b9a1dc4619aa367da811ce4e8cb2205b1") (content-digest . "5497871222ab159129a68be5fcc2c2efa03d8a38b9f7b9b0013b0782eedb281c") (timestamp . "2026-09-21T16:20:00Z") (scope . "full implementation diff main (69647f1ce5d36798e790b1d62a3b79c62b8b011f) ... head 220f676b9a1dc4619aa367da811ce4e8cb2205b1 for v1.00.31 W2 evidence identity and digest integrity (register F2/F3/F4 plus the F12 sentinel close-out): scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt (new tool: digest/verify/bind/record-commit with typed verdicts digest-ok/digest-mismatch/malformed-digest/pure/impure-record-commit, the check alias of verify demanded literally by the wave contract, GIT_*-scrubbed git subprocesses, long-form :(exclude) magic pathspecs byte-identical to scripts/gsd-delivery.py digest()); scripts/gsd-wave-gate.rkt (--receipt-head cross-check emitting head-binding-mismatch naming both SHAs for implementation-sha and reviewed-sha, conditional so historical trios stay readable; sentinel deny-list with typed placeholder-evidence; substantive minimum content on review scope/report and red-first.failure with typed insufficient-review-content; CLI main returns instead of exiting in-process); extensions/gsd/delivery-receipt.rkt (durable-receipt-head accessor); scripts/gsd-delivery.py (prepare() record-commit purity refusal wired to the shared tool, finalized read_staged_trio reviewer-identity assertion against the sentinel deny-list); tests/test-gsd-evidence-bind.rkt, tests/test-gsd-wave-gate-digest.rkt, tests/test-gsd-wave-gate.rkt (red-first fixtures with refusal AND control directions); tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt (falsifiable F2/F3/F4 guards asserting both directions); tests/test-gsd-delivery-receipt.rkt (durable-receipt-head both directions); tests/helpers/w2-mini-git-repo.rkt (hermetic mini git fixture scrubbing GIT_* on every invocation); tests/test-gsd-delivery-controller.py (mixed-commit and sentinel-refuser fixtures with truthful second-PR base); tests/test-gsd-governance-workflow.rkt (pass-fixture narratives lengthened to meet the contract-mandated minimum-content floors); artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w2/** (evidence-integrity matrix with verdict lines extracted verbatim from the raw captures, four red-first captures, SHA256SUMS, retained fast RUN-SUMMARY), reports/test-ownership-map.*, README.md (metrics resync), docs/reports/EVIDENCE-INTEGRITY-v1.00.31.md (wave report).") (report . "Two review rounds. (1) 3c37f443 -> APPROVED with four non-blocking findings; three were acted on before the next head: the wave contract's literal --check mode is now delivered as the check subcommand (a fail-closed alias of verify listed in the usage text and pinned by a new both-directions test, closing the dead --check parse the round flagged); a duplicated require block in the CLI test was merged; and the report documents the two dispositioned observations - refusal verdicts deliberately exit 0 with typed codes on stdout (nonzero exit is reserved for tool failure, consumers parse stdout, recorded as an F8-adjacent ergonomics note) and the binding-time review() reconciliation in scripts/gsd-delivery.py that accepts a reviewed-sha which is an evidence-only ancestor of the receipt head, which is what allows a pre-merge reviewed head to be bound to the post-merge receipt and stays fail-closed through require_receipt_tip on any non-evidence drift. (2) 220f676b (this head) -> APPROVED: the delta was exactly the three fixes and the report update, the round-1 substance was re-verified intact (typed verdicts, hermetic git subprocesses, exclusion contract, gate refusals, purity wiring, register guards pinned to exactly F1-F4), and the three remaining observations (exit-0 ergonomics, no production caller yet passes --receipt-head because production head binding is enforced by the coordinator/expected-head path the wave contract explicitly permits, and record-commit-purity scanning only commits that touch the evidence record directory) are recorded as informational with the report carrying the same statements, not smoothed over. The reviewer verified the F2 exclusion contract is byte-identical to the Python digest contract and that the empty-tree property reproduces the W1 publication range through the new tool."))